<!--
Cross-machine HiL (controller.launch.py on Jetson + host.launch.py on desktop) over a direct
Ethernet link.

Root cause found by capture (`tcpdump -i eth0 port 17900`) + `netstat -s` on the Jetson: CycloneDDS's
SPDP discovery payload is ~13.5KB (ROS2 nodes register a lot of parameter-service DDS endpoints),
which is well over the ~1472-byte Ethernet MTU payload and so gets IP-fragmented into ~10 packets.
`netstat -s` showed most fragment reassemblies failing (only ~12% succeeded) -- small single-packet
tools (`ros2 multicast send/receive`, plain `nc`) never fragment and so never hit this, which is
why they worked while real DDS discovery silently didn't. NIC offload (GRO/GSO/TSO) was a red
herring, ruled out by disabling it on both ends with no change.

Fix: cap CycloneDDS's own datagram size below the path MTU so it does its own reliable RTPS-level
fragmentation (retried, reassembled within DDS) instead of relying on best-effort IP fragmentation.
This is the standard fix for exactly this symptom on any lossy/unusual link.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain>
    <General>
      <FragmentSize>1344B</FragmentSize>
    </General>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
